# Per-expert kernel dispatch integration: wire moe_expert_swiglu.cl into
# the live dispatch path (campaign: sub4bit-vram-kernel).
#
# Design:   docs/design-routing-aware-expert-execution.md §2, §2.5
# Campaign: docs/campaigns/sub4bit-vram-kernel.md
# Gate:     a model with >= 512 experts serves on one card with routing-aware
#           expert execution: only the routed experts computed per token.
#
# Prerequisite patches:
#   0038 — per-expert dispatch framework (blanket sentinel, CPU-tier redirect)
#   0039 — per-expert OCL kernel (moe_expert_swiglu.cl)
#
# This patch wires them together: GPU-resident experts are dispatched to the
# per-expert OCL kernel (expert_gate_up, expert_down), non-resident experts
# go to the CPU tier (patch 0011), and the fused GEMV path is bypassed for
# all top-k experts via sentinels.
#
# The mechanism, step by step:
#   1. try_acquire_simultaneous runs NORMALLY (patch 0038's blanket-sentinel
#      block is removed). GPU LRU cache residents get real slot indices;
#      non-residents get kCpuTierSentinelSlot + cpu_tier_misses.
#   2. on_before_batched_gemv builds a _gpu_dispatches vector from the lease:
#      each non-sentinel entry becomes {slot_index, topk_position, flat_id}.
#   3. ALL top-k positions in expert_index_buffer are written as sentinels,
#      so the fused GEMV kernels (mlp_gate_up, mlp_down) skip every top-k
#      expert. The shared expert (if any) is NOT sentineled and still runs
#      through the fused path.
#   4. For each GPU dispatch, exec_batched_gemv launches expert_gate_up then
#      expert_down via execute_stage, passing the slot pool buffers plus
#      scalar {slot_index, element_offsets}. The kernel offsets weight/scale/zp
#      pointers by slot_index * per_expert_stride (computed from JIT
#      constants).
#   5. CPU tier: non-resident misses still go through dispatch_cpu_tier /
#      cpu_tier_join (patch 0012), exactly as before.
#   6. mlp_reduce runs unchanged over all EXPERTS_PER_TOKEN rows of scratch.y,
#      which now contain: GPU kernel results for residents, CPU tier results
#      for non-residents, shared expert result from the fused path.
#
# Kernel changes (moe_expert_swiglu.cl):
#   FAKE_GROUP_SIZE is derived from JIT constants (GATE_UP_GROUP_SIZE,
#   DOWN_GROUP_SIZE) using the same min(group_sizes, 128) logic as the fused
#   kernel. Both entry points are guarded by #ifdef GATE_UP_ENABLE / DOWN_ENABLE
#   so a single compilation unit produces only one kernel (C3 fix).
#
#   expert_gate_up gains three scalar parameters: slot_index (int),
#   x_base_elem (int), y_base_elem (int). The kernel offsets each weight/
#   scale/zp pointer by slot_index * per_expert_stride (long arithmetic to
#   avoid overflow at 512 slots), reads input at x[x_base_elem + ...], and
#   writes output at y[y_base_elem + token_idx * INTERMEDIATE_SIZE]. gws[0]=1
#   because each dispatch handles one (token, expert) pair (C4 fix).
#
#   expert_down gains four scalar parameters: slot_index (int), x_base_elem,
#   rw_base_elem, y_base_elem (all int). Same pointer offsetting. Reads input
#   at x[x_base_elem + ...], routing weight at routing_weights[rw_base_elem +
#   token_idx], writes at y[y_base_elem + ...].
#
# Per-expert strides, all computable from JIT constants:
#   gate/up weight (uchar): INTERMEDIATE_SIZE * HIDDEN_SIZE / 2
#   gate/up scale  (half):  (HIDDEN_SIZE / GATE_UP_GROUP_SIZE) * INTERMEDIATE_SIZE
#   gate/up zp     (uchar): (HIDDEN_SIZE / GATE_UP_GROUP_SIZE) * INTERMEDIATE_SIZE / 2
#   down weight    (uchar): HIDDEN_SIZE * INTERMEDIATE_SIZE / 2
#   down scale     (half):  (INTERMEDIATE_SIZE / DOWN_GROUP_SIZE) * HIDDEN_SIZE
#   down zp        (uchar): (INTERMEDIATE_SIZE / DOWN_GROUP_SIZE) * HIDDEN_SIZE / 2
#
# Maximum byte offset at 512 slots: 511 * 819200 = 418 MB, fits in signed
# int32 (max 2.1 GB). Long cast in the kernel is for the multiplication
# intermediate, not the final offset.
#
# Perf counter: per_expert_gpu_invocations += 2 * gpu_dispatches.size()
# (one gate_up + one down per resident expert). Distinguishes GPU kernel use
# from CPU-tier fallback (per_expert_dispatches counts both).
#
# Event ordering: in-order OCL queue (execution_config.cpp forces in_order
# whenever use_onednn is set). All per-expert kernels are enqueued after the
# fused stages (which no-op via sentinels) and before cpu_tier_join / reduce.
# Program order on the in-order queue is sufficient.
#
# KernelGenerator stages (MoEExpertGateUp, MoEExpertDown) are member-
# initialized at class scope, so make_deep_copy correctly creates fresh
# stages in the clone (M1 fix). u4 weight type assertion at init time
# guards against untested dtype paths (M2 fix). Memory pointers use
# auto (not auto*) for shared_ptr returns (C2 fix).
#
# Applied against the pinned runtime, build 2026.4.0-22849-71640275d29, on
# top of patches/0003-0039.

